CC0 1.0 Universal — Public Domain Dedication
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

The source registry in this directory — every manifest, the organization
table, and the capability vocabulary — is dedicated to the public domain.

This is deliberate and it is the point. What the registry encodes is an
inventory: which public systems exist across DOE and its seventeen national
laboratories, who stewards each one, who funds it, what its terms say, what
it does not cover, and what is blocking the ones that are not wired up yet.
That inventory took the research recorded in this repository's research/
directory to assemble, and it is more useful to the world unencumbered than
it is as anything this project owns.

Take it. Fork it, machine-read it, build a competing set of servers on it,
or fold it into a government system. No attribution is required, though a
pointer back is welcome so corrections can find their way home.

The code that reads this registry is Apache-2.0 (see ../LICENSE). Data
retrieved FROM the systems described here carries its own publisher's terms,
recorded per source in each manifest and in ../THIRD_PARTY_DATA.yml.
